          "final_text_tail": "`; value is coerced to `float` and stored as `self.cleanup_timeout`\n- `Context.close()` (src/click/core.py:638): with a timeout set, cleanup runs in a daemon thread via `_close_stack_with_timeout()`; on expiry a `WARNING` is logged on the `click.core` logger and `close()` returns (graceful degradation, no hang); cleanup errors that finish in time are re-raised (parity with the unbounded path). Without a timeout, behavior is unchanged.\n\n`src/click/shell_completion.py`\n- `ShellComplete.get_completions` now closes the resolved context chain in a `finally` block via the new `_close_context_chain()` helper (leaf-first to root), so cleanup registered during completion actually runs \u2014 and is bounded, since subcontexts inherit `cleanup_timeout` from the root context that receives it via `ctx_args` (e.g. `main(cleanup_timeout=5.0)`).\n\n**Verified**\n- Hanging close callback (10s sleep) with `cleanup_timeout=0.5`: `close()` returns in ~0.5s, warning logged (captured via `caplog` and `assertLogs(\"click\")`/`(\"click.core\")`); fast cleanups still run and still raise; `with ctx:` exit path bounded; subcontext inheritance works.\n- Completion with a hanging cleanup + `cleanup_timeout=1.0` returns in ~1.0s with correct output.\n- Full suite: 558 passed, 21 skipped, 1 xfailed. `test_basic.py` has a pre-existing pytest-version collection error (confirmed identical with changes stashed). `test_imports.py` passes \u2014 `logging` is lazy-imported only on the timeout path (`threading` is in the allowlist).",
